Jahshaka patch 0045 — the cone diffuse and an irradiance field over PART of it.

MEDIA-only patch (one Hlms piece). Studio stages its media from the SOURCE tree
(cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake), so every tree still has to re-run
`irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` to get it — no engine rebuild is needed beyond the
staging. It OVERLAPS patches 0021 and 0033 (and HDR-1's 0043 in a neighbouring file) in the same file: a tree that already
carries those hits `build-ogre.sh`'s "Upstream changed the patched file" on a
re-run, which is the documented per-patch reverse-check blind spot and NOT an
upstream change. The cure is the recorded one — reset the submodule
(`git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- . && git ... clean -fd`) and
re-run the script.

WHY. `HlmsPbs::preparePassHash` sets `vct_disable_diffuse` whenever an
irradiance field is bound (OgreHlmsPbs.cpp:1846-1850), because upstream's field
covers the whole voxel volume: the cones would compute the same diffuse term a
second time. Jahshaka's Photon arm puts the field on the INNERMOST cascade of a
chain (PHOTON_SPEC E1), where that is no longer true — the field covers a 10 m
box and the cascades around it hold real, voxelised, light-injected radiance out
to the outermost box. Scene-wide "field instead of cones" would leave every pixel
in the ring with specular cones and ambient and no diffuse bounce at all, which
is the reason the outer cascades exist.

So under a chain the engine's own Hlms listener re-opens the gate
(FogHlmsListener::propertiesMergedPreGenerationStep, derived from the properties
`irradiance_field` and `vct_num_probes` so the shader cache stays consistent) and
the two terms are blended BY THE FIELD'S CONFIDENCE — the field inside the
cascade it rides, the cones outside it, never both. The blend itself lives in
Jahshaka's own `JahIfd_piece_ps.any`, which is inserted immediately after
`applyVoxelConeTracing` in the same scope (Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any:966-967)
and so can read `vctDiffuse` directly.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES is only that hand-off: where a field is bound, the cone
diffuse is NOT accumulated here, because the piece that runs next accumulates it
weighted. It is a two-line change plus its rationale, and it is inert for
upstream's arrangement (with one volume, `vct_disable_diffuse` is set and the
whole block is absent from the generated shader).

Verified: `git apply --check` against the pin with patches 0001-0044 applied and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane
worktree; the `--engine-selftest` hash unchanged (the default scene is one
volume, where this block does not exist).

--- a/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any
@@ -641,7 +641,22 @@
 					 OGRE_VCT_ANISO_ROOT_PROBE_ARG );
 
 	@property( !vct_disable_diffuse )
-		pixelData.envColourD.xyz += vctDiffuse.xyz;
+		@property( irradiance_field )
+			// Jahshaka patch 0045: an irradiance field over PART of what the
+			// cones cover. With a cascade chain the field rides the innermost
+			// cascade only, so the cone diffuse is the answer for every pixel
+			// the field cannot reach and the two must be blended rather than
+			// one of them chosen scene-wide. The blend is by the field's own
+			// confidence and it lives in Jahshaka's JahIfd piece, which runs
+			// immediately after this one, in this same scope, and reads
+			// `vctDiffuse` from here.
+			//
+			// Nothing changes for upstream's own arrangement: with one volume
+			// HlmsPbs sets vct_disable_diffuse for any bound field and this
+			// whole block is absent from the generated shader.
+		@else
+			pixelData.envColourD.xyz += vctDiffuse.xyz;
+		@end
 	@end
 	@property( !vct_disable_specular )
 		pixelData.envColourS.xyz += vctSpecular.xyz;
